# Readapaper — example env (dummy values; copy to .env.local and fill in).
#
# KINDLE SETUP (§7 — the v0 setup doc lives here so no new top-level doc file
# is needed):
#
# 1. Find your Kindle address ("Send-to-Kindle Email"):
#    Amazon → Account → Content & Devices → Devices → pick your Kindle →
#    the address looks like name@kindle.com (or @kindle.cn / @free.kindle.com
#    for older devices). That value goes in KINDLE_EMAIL below.
# 2. Approve the sender: Amazon → Account → Content & Devices → Preferences →
#    Personal Document Settings → "Approved Personal Document E-mail List" →
#    add FROM_EMAIL verbatim. Amazon silently drops mail from unapproved
#    senders, so a "sent but never arrived" doc almost always means this step
#    was skipped.
# 3. SMTP notes (Gmail style): Gmail no longer accepts your login password for
#    SMTP — create an App Password (Google Account → Security → 2-Step
#    Verification → App passwords), then use SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com,
#    SMTP_PORT=587, SMTP_SECURE=false, SMTP_USER=you@gmail.com,
#    SMTP_PASS=<16-char app password>. Outlook/others need the provider's
#    SMTP host/port and an app password or equivalent; plain passwords usually
#    fail. Never commit the real password — keep it in .env.local only.
# 4. .env.local example:
#      SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
#      SMTP_PORT=587
#      SMTP_SECURE=false
#      SMTP_USER=you@gmail.com
#      SMTP_PASS=xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx
#      KINDLE_EMAIL=name@kindle.com
#      FROM_EMAIL=you@gmail.com
# 5. Verify: (a) GET /api/kindle/status → {"configured":true,...} (no secrets
#    in the response); (b) save an article, click "Send 50 latest to Kindle";
#    (c) check the Kindle library — documents arrive as "Readapaper Kindle
#    Export" (wireless delivery may take a few minutes).
# 6. v0 limits: one compiled HTML attachment per send, latest 50 active
#    (non-archived, newest first) articles; batches over ~40MB are refused
#    (under Amazon's 50MB mail cap with headroom) with an error suggesting
#    fewer/more-recent articles — no multi-mail splitting in v0.

SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_SECURE=false
SMTP_USER=you@example.com
SMTP_PASS=example-app-password
KINDLE_EMAIL=name@kindle.com
FROM_EMAIL=you@example.com
